  "causalSequence": [
    "boil peeled potatoes in salted water until very tender, 15-20 min",
    "brown lamb mince, in batches; drain excess fat",
    "soften onion, carrot (celery/fennel) in same pan, 5-10 min",
    "add garlic; cook 1-2 min",
    "stir in tomato paste or flour to thicken",
    "add stock, worcestershire, herbs; simmer until thick, 10-45 min",
    "stir in peas (and corn) near end",
    "drain potatoes; mash with butter and warmed milk/cream; season",
    "spread filling in baking dish; top evenly with mash; rough peaks or cheese on top",
    "bake 180-200C until golden, 15-30 min",
    "rest 5-10 min; serve"
  ],
  "techniqueFacts": [
    "browning order varies: mince first then vegetables (s0, s2) vs vegetables first then mince (s1)",
    "thickening lever varies: 45 min open reduction (s0), tomato paste + 10 min reduction (s1), flour coating on the vegetables (s2)",
    "batch-browning the mince so it colours rather than stews (s0)",
    "peas go in late so they hold colour and texture (s1, s2)",
    "surface texture drives browning: wavy peaks in the mash (s2) or a parmesan sprinkle (s0); optional broiler/grill finish (s2)",
